<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity (Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris))",
        "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity faithfully reproduces Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py, docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 60.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif> ;
    schema:about "Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D hydrodynamic polyp-scale morphogenesis or direct statistical fitting to raw field colony time series",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact 1-year discrete volume-step algebraic functions for hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness flat disc, and fixed-diameter cylinder (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`), 6-panel comparative figure, and 15-year log-area animation",
        "reported_in_source: Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024): colony volume increment V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho implies that surface-area productivity (SAP = dS/S) and linear extension C are governed by how S:V scales with colony size across hemispheroids, cones, flat discs, and cylinders",
        "transfer_boundary: Uses a finite 1-year step V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho without comparing against the continuum differential limit (dV/dt = G*S/rho, where hemisphere dR/dt = G/rho is strictly constant at all radii), and uses schematic 2D matplotlib patches rather than 3D coral colony meshes or empirical growth time series" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif; output: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png; organism: Scleractinian reef corals (massive Porites, branching Acropora, plating Leptoseris); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; artifact_sha256: fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024): colony volume increment V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho implies that surface-area productivity (SAP = dS/S) and linear extension C are governed by how S:V scales with colony size across hemispheroids, cones, flat discs, and cylinders; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 1-year discrete volume-step algebraic functions for hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness flat disc, and fixed-diameter cylinder (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`), 6-panel comparative figure, and 15-year log-area animation; transfer_boundary: Uses a finite 1-year step V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho without comparing against the continuum differential limit (dV/dt = G*S/rho, where hemisphere dR/dt = G/rho is strictly constant at all radii), and uses schematic 2D matplotlib patches rather than 3D coral colony meshes or empirical growth time series; does_not_claim: 3D hydrodynamic polyp-scale morphogenesis or direct statistical fitting to raw field colony time series]; other sources: coral_geometry_modeling — reference code and analysis <https://github.com/ericodle/coral_geometry_modeling>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj.17037> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-4> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.02e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace (Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats))",
        "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace faithfully reproduces Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py, docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 43.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif> ;
    schema:about "Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Direct comparison to digitized Yellowstone mat or Proterozoic Conophyton thin-section photographs or empirical cone-spacing histograms",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic diffusion-length spacing law ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) for alpha in {1.0, 0.30}, hexagonal close-packed cone lattice, and a 2D Lagrangian polyline front advancing by lambda * n_hat + v * w_photic * z_hat with pinned basal endpoints and 3-point Laplacian smoothing",
        "reported_in_source: Batchelor et al. (2004): deterministic KPZ / normal-plus-vertical lamina accretion dh/dt = v + lambda * (1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2) transitions from domes to cones as beta = v / lambda increases",
        "reported_in_source: Petroff et al. (2010): nutrient diffusion over active photosynthetic period tau sets inter-cone spacing ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) (~1 cm for daily cycle), and diffusive flux gradients along the mat interface govern lamina accretion and conical geometry",
        "transfer_boundary: The dome-to-cone lamina solver does not solve Petroff et al.'s Laplace diffusion equation (nabla^2 c = 0) or local diffusive flux; it substitutes a modified Batchelor et al. (2004) kinematic front with an ad-hoc photic weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "10. Stigmergy & Active Swarms" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Conical Microbial Laminae" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Diffusive Spacing Lambda" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Slime Molds & Bacteria" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Cyanobacteria" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif; output: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png; organism: Photosynthetic microbial mats and conical stromatolites (Conophyton / Yellowstone modern mats); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; artifact_sha256: 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Petroff et al. (2010): nutrient diffusion over active photosynthetic period tau sets inter-cone spacing ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) (~1 cm for daily cycle), and diffusive flux gradients along the mat interface govern lamina accretion and conical geometry | Batchelor et al. (2004): deterministic KPZ / normal-plus-vertical lamina accretion dh/dt = v + lambda * (1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2) transitions from domes to cones as beta = v / lambda increases; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic diffusion-length spacing law ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) for alpha in {1.0, 0.30}, hexagonal close-packed cone lattice, and a 2D Lagrangian polyline front advancing by lambda * n_hat + v * w_photic * z_hat with pinned basal endpoints and 3-point Laplacian smoothing; transfer_boundary: The dome-to-cone lamina solver does not solve Petroff et al.'s Laplace diffusion equation (nabla^2 c = 0) or local diffusive flux; it substitutes a modified Batchelor et al. (2004) kinematic front with an ad-hoc photic weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2; does_not_claim: Direct comparison to digitized Yellowstone mat or Proterozoic Conophyton thin-section photographs or empirical cone-spacing histograms]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physa.2004.01.065>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1001978107> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-4> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Mathematical Morphogenesis Model" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 4.36e-01 .

