<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every geometric function states its exact volume $V$, active calcifying surface area $S$, and resulting one-step algebraic relation in its docstring, and the module docstring summarizes the four geometries' $(S:V, C, \\text{SAP})$ scaling regimes in a table mapped to Appendix A / Results and Figs. 3 & 6 of Kahng et al. (2024). Deduct 15 points because exact equation numbers from Kahng et al. (2024) Appendix A are not cited per function, and deduct 10 points because the distinction between discrete 1-yr difference equations and continuous ODE rates is not noted in `hemisphere_extension`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All seven algebraic functions (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`, L68-110) are exact consequences of the paper's discrete annual volume rule `V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho` under the stated surface/volume formulas (`V = 2/3 pi r^3, S = 2 pi r^2`; `V = h pi r^2, S = pi r^2`; `V = pi h^3/(3 alpha^2), S = pi h^2 sqrt(1+alpha^2)/alpha^2`; `V = pi r^2 L, S = 2 pi r L`). Deduct 14 points because the script does not contrast the finite 1-yr step (`r(t+1) - r(t)`, which rises from `0.52` to `1.20 cm/yr` in Panel c) against the instantaneous continuum limit `dr/dt = G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr` (where hemisphere linear extension is strictly size-independent); and deduct 12 points because general oblate/prolate hemispheroids and multi-branch colony self-shading are simplified to a spherical hemisphere and single cylinder without explicit boundary notes." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Morphometric validation: 38/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Computes and reports asymptotic linear extensions (`1.28 cm/yr` for massive *Porites*; `2.00, 2.53, 3.99, 7.36 cm/yr` for *Acropora* cones with `alpha = 0.5..4`), size-independent SAP (`0.114 /yr` for *Leptoseris* disc; `7.143 /yr` for *Acropora* cylinder), and the `18.9x` (`~19x`) microfragmentation SAP ratio between `r = 1 cm` (`1.86 /yr`) and `r = 25 cm` (`0.10 /yr`). Deduct 42 points because no empirical colony growth dataset (e.g., Lough 2008 *Porites* cores, Hughes 1987 *Acropora*, or Kahng 2023 *Leptoseris* measurements) is loaded to compute residuals or $R^2$; and deduct 20 points because no CSV table or automated `--self-test` verification is emitted." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-branching-acropora-cylinder-size-independent-sap-r-0-50-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-deep-water-leptoseris-flat-disc-size-independent-sap-h-0-20-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-massive-porites-hemisphere-linear-extension-c-at-r-30-cm-discrete-1-yr-step>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-measurement-massive-porites-microfragmentation-sap-speedup-ratio-r-1-cm-vs-r-25-cm>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — MorphoEval overall 60.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py` faithfully encodes the discrete annual volume-accretion master rule `V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho` and the four idealized geometric families from Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) (hemispheroid, cone, flat disc, and cylinder), reproducing their surface-area productivity (`SAP = dS/S`), linear extension (`C`), aspect-ratio dependence (Fig. 3), diameter/thickness scaling, and the ~19x microfragmentation SAP speedup for massive *Porites* (`r = 1 cm` vs `r = 25 cm`). Its main limitations are that the finite 1-year step introduces small-radius curvature in hemisphere/cone extension (`C = 0.52 -> 1.25 cm/yr` vs the exact continuum `dr/dt = G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr`), the equal-`G, rho` comparison applies `G = 1.50 g cm^-2 yr^-1` to a thin `h = 0.5 cm` disc (producing `26 cm/yr` extension at `r = 30 cm`), and no empirical colony growth tables or coral specimen photographs are overlaid. Overall 60.2/100 (faithfulness 54.6, reproducibility 73.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 74, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 38, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 72. Output judged: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/png, 282553 B, 1774×1267 px, artifact_sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812 (sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; artifact_sha256: fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024): colony volume increment V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho implies that surface-area productivity (SAP = dS/S) and linear extension C are governed by how S:V scales with colony size across hemispheroids, cones, flat discs, and cylinders; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 1-year discrete volume-step algebraic functions for hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness flat disc, and fixed-diameter cylinder (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`), 6-panel comparative figure, and 15-year log-area animation; transfer_boundary: Uses a finite 1-year step V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho without comparing against the continuum differential limit (dV/dt = G*S/rho, where hemisphere dR/dt = G/rho is strictly constant at all radii), and uses schematic 2D matplotlib patches rather than 3D coral colony meshes or empirical growth time series; does_not_claim: 3D hydrodynamic polyp-scale morphogenesis or direct statistical fitting to raw field colony time series." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:68-110,172-185 Plot the exact continuum differential extension rates (dr/dt = G/rho for hemisphere, dh/dt = G*sqrt(1+alpha^2)/rho for cone, dr/dt = G*r/(2*rho*h) for disc) alongside the discrete 1-year Euler step curves, and use realistic DISC parameters (or dual y-axes) in Panel (c).",
        "remediation needed: Vendor `datasets/kahng/` with SHA-256-pinned empirical growth tables from Lough (2008), Hughes (1987), and Kahng (2023) / Kahng et al. (2024), overlay observed colony extension/SAP data points, and add `--self-test` and CSV metrics export." ;
    pk:hasScore 6.02e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

