    dct:description "Panel (a) draws clear 2D geometric glyphs annotated with `(V, S, S:V trend)` for the four coral growth forms, Panels (b-e) reproduce the analytical curves of Kahng et al. (2024) (including Fig. 3 cone aspect ratios and Fig. 6 shape comparisons), and the GIF animates 15 years of hemisphere and cone cross-sectional growth alongside log surface-area trajectories. Deduct 35 points because no real coral colony photographs, CT-scanned 3D colony meshes, or digitized empirical data points from *Porites*, *Acropora*, or *Leptoseris* are overlaid; and deduct 23 points because in Panel (c) and the GIF, applying `COMMON` (`G=1.50, rho=1.20`) to a `0.5 cm` flat disc drives disc extension to `26.1 cm/yr` at `r = 30 cm` and area to `~10^9 cm^2` at year 15, visually dwarfing the realistic hemisphere and cone curves." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
