<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 44/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Correctly evaluates the diffusive spacing relation `ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau)` (L64-67) and hexagonal lattice geometry (L70-81). However, (-22) the lamina cross-section model (L113-163) does not solve Petroff et al.'s (2010) diffusive nutrient field (`nabla^2 c = 0`) or flux-driven lamina growth (`v_n prop dc/dn`), so the top row (diffusion spacing) and bottom row (lamina shapes) are mathematically uncoupled; (-14) relative to the Batchelor et al. (2004) equation cited in the docstring (`dh/dt = v + lambda*(1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2)`, L34, L296), `_advance_front` introduces an uncited quadratic photic crest weight `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88 * (z / z.max())**2` (L130), pins the basal endpoints at `+-base_half` (L136-137), and applies a 3-point Laplacian smoothing filter (L141-142); and (-8) the text panel states that `ell ~ 0.66 cm` records a `~20 h` rhythmic metabolism (L238-239) whereas `0.66 cm` was computed from `tau = 12 h` (L193, L235)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 4.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

