<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — MorphoEval overall 43.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`2010-petroff-stromatolite.py` implements Petroff et al.'s (2010) diffusion-competition spacing formula `ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau)` (`ell = 0.66 cm` at `tau = 12 h`, `D = 1e-5 cm^2/s`, `alpha = 1.0`), renders a hexagonal packing diagram, and sweeps `beta = v/lambda` across `{0.3, 1.5, 5.0}` (and `0.2 -> 6.0` in the 70-frame GIF) to illustrate the transition from squat domes (`H/W = 0.67`) to tall cones (`H/W = 2.62`). However, the lamina growth model is not Petroff et al.'s diffusive-flux solver (`nabla^2 c = 0` with growth proportional to normal flux `dc/dn`), nor is it an exact integration of the Batchelor et al. (2004) KPZ equation printed in the docstring: it advances a pinned-base Lagrangian front with an unsourced quadratic crest-weighting `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2` and 3-point smoothing, and compares against no empirical stromatolite thin sections or measured spacing distributions. Overall 43.6/100 (faithfulness 37.2, reproducibility 58.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 44, Morphological realism / specimen match 30, Parameter expressivity 60, Morphometric validation 25, Source and data traceability 52, Code-to-model traceability 50, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/png, 328721 B, 1736×1244 px, artifact_sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01 (sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; artifact_sha256: 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Petroff et al. (2010): nutrient diffusion over active photosynthetic period tau sets inter-cone spacing ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) (~1 cm for daily cycle), and diffusive flux gradients along the mat interface govern lamina accretion and conical geometry | Batchelor et al. (2004): deterministic KPZ / normal-plus-vertical lamina accretion dh/dt = v + lambda * (1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2) transitions from domes to cones as beta = v / lambda increases; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic diffusion-length spacing law ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) for alpha in {1.0, 0.30}, hexagonal close-packed cone lattice, and a 2D Lagrangian polyline front advancing by lambda * n_hat + v * w_photic * z_hat with pinned basal endpoints and 3-point Laplacian smoothing; transfer_boundary: The dome-to-cone lamina solver does not solve Petroff et al.'s Laplace diffusion equation (nabla^2 c = 0) or local diffusive flux; it substitutes a modified Batchelor et al. (2004) kinematic front with an ad-hoc photic weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2; does_not_claim: Direct comparison to digitized Yellowstone mat or Proterozoic Conophyton thin-section photographs or empirical cone-spacing histograms." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:126-143,238-239 Document or remove the ad-hoc photic weighting `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z.max())**2`, release or widen the pinned basal footprint for the dome regime (`beta = 0.3`), and reconcile the `tau = 12 h` calculation (`ell = 0.66 cm`) with the `~20 h` text annotation.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:86-163 Implement Petroff et al.'s (2010) steady-state nutrient diffusion field (nabla^2 c = 0 around periodic absorbing cones with normal velocity proportional to local diffusive flux dc/dn), and clearly separate it from the Batchelor et al. (2004) KPZ / Lagrangian front model.",
        "remediation needed: Create `datasets/petroff/` with a SHA-256-pinned transcription of Petroff et al.'s measured modern, lab, and fossil cone spacings plus a segmented *Conophyton* thin-section profile, and add `--self-test` and CSV metrics export." ;
    pk:hasScore 4.36e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
